# `.env.testing` — template for the REQUIRED secret keys
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# `.env.testing` is loaded automatically when APP_ENV=testing (see phpunit.xml, which
# pins APP_ENV=testing). It used to be committed to Git CONTAINING REAL CREDENTIALS:
# APP_KEY, DB_PASSWORD, MAIL_PASSWORD, RAZORPAY_KEY, RAZORPAY_SECRET and REDIS_PASSWORD
# were byte-identical to the values in the developer's working `.env`.
#
# Those values have been stripped from `.env.testing`. Secrets are now supplied by the
# real process environment instead, which is the standard CI pattern and keeps credentials
# out of version control entirely.
#
# Laravel's Dotenv is IMMUTABLE: a variable that already exists in the environment is NOT
# overwritten by any .env file. So exporting these keys always wins over `.env.testing`.
#
# Required to run the test suite
# ------------------------------
#   DB_USERNAME      test database user
#   DB_PASSWORD      test database password
#   RAZORPAY_KEY     Razorpay key id   (only for GoldenApiContractRegressionTest,
#   RAZORPAY_SECRET  Razorpay secret    "payment order create contract and auth")
#
# Everything else the suite needs is already non-secret and lives in `.env.testing`
# (APP_ENV, DB_DATABASE, driver switches) or in `phpunit.xml`
# (CACHE_STORE=array, SESSION_DRIVER=array, QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync, BCRYPT_ROUNDS=4).
#
# Running the suite
# -----------------
#   source .env.testing.local   # or: ./vendor/bin/... ; see below
#   php artisan test
#
# `.env.testing.local` is a git-ignored helper that re-exports the DB and payment
# credentials from your private `.env`, plus overrides DB_DATABASE to the TEST
# database. It is NOT committed, because it would reintroduce the leak this file
# documents. Create it once:
#
#   { set -a; . ./.env; set +a; export DB_DATABASE=db_illuvision_testing; } \
#       > .env.testing.local
#   echo '.env.testing.local' >> .gitignore   # already ignored
#
# In CI, configure these as repository secrets and map them into the job environment.
#
# ROTATION REQUIRED
# -----------------
# Removing the values from the working tree does NOT remove them from Git history. Every
# credential listed above that was ever committed must be treated as compromised and
# ROTATED at the provider. See docs/audit/phase-0.21-final-report.md.
